<div class="privacy-document">
  <section>
    <h2>Privacy Policy</h2>
    <p><strong>App:</strong> Equation Grid</p>
    <p><strong>Effective Date:</strong> August 29, 2026</p>
    <p>Equation Grid is an offline mathematical crossword game. This policy explains what information the app handles when you use it.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>1. Information We Collect</h2>
    <p>Equation Grid does not require an account and does not ask you to provide personal information. The app does not include its own advertising, analytics, or online account system.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>2. Information Stored on Your Device</h2>
    <p>To provide the game experience, Equation Grid stores progress, best times, onboarding status, sound effects, haptics, and theme preferences locally on your device.</p>
    <p>This information is not uploaded by Equation Grid to a server.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>3. Sharing and External Services</h2>
    <p>If you choose <strong>Share the app</strong>, Android opens the system share sheet. The app you select may handle the shared message according to its own privacy policy.</p>
    <p>Equation Grid does not control or receive data handled by those external apps.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>4. Internet Access</h2>
    <p>The core game and saved progress are designed to work without an internet connection.</p>
    <p>The availability of external features, such as sharing or accessing a store listing, may depend on Android and the services you choose to open.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>5. Children’s Privacy</h2>
    <p>Equation Grid does not knowingly request personal information from children.</p>
    <p>Because the app does not require an account, please do not enter personal information into any free-form field if a future version adds one.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>6. Data Deletion</h2>
    <p>You can remove locally stored game progress from <strong>Settings &gt; Reset progress</strong>.</p>
    <p>You can also remove all app data through Android system settings by uninstalling the app or clearing the app’s storage.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>7. Changes to This Policy</h2>
    <p>This policy may be updated when the app’s data practices change. The effective date above will be updated with a revised version.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>8. Contact</h2>
    <p>For privacy questions, contact the developer using the contact details provided on the Equation Grid Google Play listing.</p>
  </section>
</div>

